<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
     AresLauncher: the marker for the RECENTS section of the app-list pane (§11b).

     A lightning bolt, at the user's suggestion: "we should also give it an icon like the letters -
     maybe a lightning bolt or something". It stands in the same slot a letter occupies, so the
     recents block reads as one of the list's own sections rather than as a block bolted above them.

     A VECTOR, deliberately, and not the ⚡ emoji codepoint. An emoji renders in the system emoji
     font: full colour, its own metrics, and a weight that has nothing to do with the letters beside
     it. A monochrome path tinted from the same colour the section headers already use sits at the
     letters' weight by construction, in both themes and against any wallpaper.

     No colour of its own for the same reason: every consumer tints it. The in-list header tints
     from the header TextView's own text colour (?attr/workspaceTextColor), and the fast-scroll
     popup tints from the popup's (?android:attr/textColorPrimaryInverse). Baking a colour in here
     would be wrong on one of them whatever it was.

     The intrinsic 14dp box is sized against the 13sp header letters. The popup overrides it with
     explicit bounds, because its letters are much larger.
-->
<vector xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:width="14dp"
    android:height="14dp"
    android:viewportWidth="24"
    android:viewportHeight="24">
    <path
        android:fillColor="@android:color/white"
        android:pathData="M7,2 L7,13 L10,13 L10,22 L17,10 L13,10 L17,2 Z" />
</vector>
